+	# ------------------------------------------------------------------
+	# The probe: what a harness may see of the engine beside its commands.
+
+	## For test platforms and harnesses: one fact of the probe. Every field
+	## is a scalar the engine holds or carries where the fact is noted; none
+	## is a value of an app, so a fact needs nothing of an app's types.
+	##
+	## The first five describe the site tree as it is stored
+	## (`Core.probe_tree`), in document order: `AtSite` opens a site, with
+	## its kind, its depth, whether its written layer still waits for a pass
+	## (for the root: whether its pending write set is not empty), the mask
+	## of the signal it reads itself (`own`) and the reads it caps a branch
+	## it has not mounted with (`cap`); `ValueHeld` is the value a `state` or
+	## a `derive` site holds, as `Str.inspect` writes it (the one fact that
+	## allocates, and only for this question); `BlockReads` is what its block says
+	## it reads; `HoleHeld` is one hole, with its mask; `ChildAt` opens child
+	## `index` with the reads its parent tests a pass against, and `Close`
+	## ends it. A kind the probe does not describe yet answers `Opaque` and
+	## nothing below it.
+	##
+	## The rest are noted while a turn runs (`Core.probe_start`), each at the
+	## call it names, in the order the engine made them: `TurnBegan` is the
+	## start of one turn (an event, a result or a follow-up); `RootPass` and
+	## `PassFrom` start a pass (at the root for cells, with their signature;
+	## at the state site at that depth), `Joined` and `Walked` are a waiting
+	## layer joining a pass and being reached by the walk after it,
+	## `Entered` and `Left` bracket a call into child `index` of the block
+	## being refreshed or routed through, `Evaluated` is one evaluation of
